<article class="env-lemma" id="0AHL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AHL">Lemma <span data-tag="0AHL">3.9.12</span>.</a> Let $\{ f_ i : X_ i \to X\} _{i \in I}$ be an fppf covering of a scheme. There exists an fppf covering $\{ W_ j \to X\} _{j \in J}$ which is a refinement of $\{ X_ i \to X\} _{i \in I}$ such that $\text{size}(\coprod W_ j) \leq \text{size}(X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose an affine open covering $X = \bigcup _{a \in A} U_ a$ with $|A| \leq \text{size}(X)$. For each $a$ we can choose a finite subset $I_ a \subset I$ and for $i \in I_ a$ a quasi-compact open $W_{a, i} \subset X_ i$ such that $U_ a = \bigcup _{i \in I_ a} f_ i(W_{a, i})$. Then $\text{size}(W_{a, i}) \leq \text{size}(X)$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/04T7" data-tag="04T7">3.9.7</a>. We conclude that $\text{size}(\coprod _ a \coprod _{i \in I_ a} W_{i, a}) \leq \text{size}(X)$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/000Q" data-tag="000Q">3.9.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>